|---|---|---|---|
| 2 | WORDING | None. | Not applicable. |

Pass-1 HIGH findings are fixed in the candidate.

`_team_pending_publication` now recognizes compact maps through the shared
`_team_publication_map` helper and, before a first remote observation, requires
the existing intake anchor and the actual pinned BASE
(`orchestrator/workflow_runtime.py:1351-1369`).
`_team_publication_intake` validates one completed `EVIDENCE_INTAKE` manifest,
its exact content-addressed output, installation/owner/epoch/BASE binding, and
the preceding INTENT then CONFIRMED checkpoint history
(`orchestrator/workflow_runtime.py:1906-1946`). It also reuses the existing
integration validator rather than adding a receipt schema. The same helper is
called at reservation (`:2055-2058`). A direct byte-correct map without intake
is rejected before observation; test `:5865-5886` passed in
`/home/chirurgie/.cache/q3-publication-provenance-r2-20260914.log`.

For the valid-private-state loss case, a syntactically valid local file with
`operations: {}` lacks the completed intake anchor and is rejected before it can
mint a replacement remote observation or reservation. The regression covers
both RESERVED and post-commit/PUSH_RESERVED state (`:5684-5738`). The required
BASE check is executed through the same pending guard before registered
observation as well as reserve (`orchestrator/workflow_runtime.py:1368-1369`).
The retained selective rollback that preserves all pre-publication anchors while
deleting only the publication receipt before local commit remains intrinsically
indistinguishable under R6's single cooperative private record; it is not a new
candidate regression or a basis for another schema.

The initial five-test provenance run had one fixture setup error, not a runtime
assertion failure: the negative fixture read a private file before creating it.
The correction adds `self.local()` before publication INTENT; the exact negative
rerun passed (1 test, 0.421 seconds). The first affected full suite had already
passed pre-anchor (218 tests, 190.104 seconds). The post-anchor full affected
suite was still running at this pass; it is not counted as green here.

