Focused confirmation:

- First observe remains legitimate only after a completed exact map intake
  (manifest/output/owner/installation/epoch/BASE, then historical INTENT and
  CONFIRMED) at `orchestrator/workflow_runtime.py:1906-1946`; the check runs
  through the pending guard before remote observation at `:1351-1369`.
- A source-only repair remains narrow: `_team_publication_repair`
  (`:1975-2010`) binds the current operation inputs to the exact repair
  candidate, independently validated FIX_VERIFIED event, assignment provenance,
  permitted paths and repair sources. The real lifecycle fixture preserves the
  separate integration review and repair review, publishes the source-only
  repair first, confirms the fresh remote commit, and only then proceeds to
  compact incoming publication (`orchestrator/tests/test_workflow_runtime.py:5930-6060`).
- A map-shaped publication that lacks its valid anchor can at most reach the
  ordinary observation/reservation surface; it cannot pass
  `_team_publication_snapshot` / native publication guard. The anchored compact
  and exact repair routes remain the only publication snapshots. This preserves
  the requested repair admission without expanding generic source-only behavior.
- Pass-2 direct-map, empty-private-state (RESERVED and PUSH_RESERVED), and
  pre-observe BASE-drift regression locators remain `:5684-5738` and
  `:5855-5886`. No source, foreign-state, revision-10 compatibility, or pinned
  engine recovery surface changed since pass 2.

Post-anchor full-suite execution was owned by the parent and was still in
progress during this pass; it is not represented as passed here. Pre-anchor
full affected suite and post-anchor targeted provenance evidence remain as
reported in pass 2. The known baseline wiring failures are not attributed to
this candidate.

